From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thinh Nguyen <Thinh.Nguyen@synopsys.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:38:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/30] usb: dwc3: gadget: Recover from End Transfer timeout

If the End Transfer command times out, the endpoint resource is never
released and every subsequent Start Transfer to the endpoint fails with
"No Resource". Schedule an error recovery to reset the controller.

Signed-off-by: Thinh Nguyen <Thinh.Nguyen@synopsys.com>
Cc: stable <stable@kernel.org>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/7523e9a11303a33acd0b92a092fb0e8218d509d2.1792542945.git.Thinh.Nguyen@synopsys.com
Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman <gregkh@linuxfoundation.org>

[mzak: picked from linux-next 61575534 (Thinh Nguyen's End Transfer series) for q91j, gains #30 (gadget path only; dwc3-qcom and its interconnect votes untouched); applies on this tree]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/gadget.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/gadget.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/gadget.c
index 33fa32fd2..a907fdfac 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/gadget.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/gadget.c
@@ -1775,6 +1775,8 @@ static int __dwc3_gadget_get_frame(struct dwc3 *dwc)
 	return DWC3_DSTS_SOFFN(reg);
 }
 
+static void dwc3_schedule_err_recovery(struct dwc3 *dwc);
+
 /**
  * __dwc3_stop_active_transfer - stop the current active transfer
  * @dep: isoc endpoint
@@ -1818,6 +1820,9 @@ static int __dwc3_stop_active_transfer(struct dwc3_ep *dep, bool force, bool int
 		dev_err_ratelimited(dep->dwc->dev,
 				"end transfer failed: %d\n", ret);
 
+	if (ret == -ETIMEDOUT && dep->dwc->err_state == DWC3_ERR_NONE)
+		dwc3_schedule_err_recovery(dep->dwc);
+
 	dep->resource_index = 0;
 
 	if (!interrupt || (ret && ret != -ETIMEDOUT))
-- 
